# HooshyarOS Cline execution rules

## Role
Cline is a local VS Code execution/operator layer. It is NOT the architecture owner and must not redefine Architecture Freeze V4, governance, product semantics, or completion rules.

## Source of truth
Always read, in order:
1. Docs/HOOSHYAROS_MASTER_CHARTER.md
2. Docs/HOOSHYAROS_GOVERNANCE_CHARTER.md
3. Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
4. Docs/COMMERCIAL_PRODUCT_COMPLETION_CONTRACT.md
5. Assistant/SYSTEM_PROMPT.md
6. Docs/Product/PRODUCT_CONSTRUCTION_ROADMAP.json
7. Docs/Product/PRODUCT_PLATFORM_MANIFEST.json
8. Docs/Product/PRODUCT_QUALIFICATION_MATRIX.json

The Manifest defines what the product is. The Qualification Matrix defines what must be proven. Never replace either with intuition.

## Mandatory execution loop
Run the real product factory, not a simulated audit:
`READ -> AUDIT -> SELECT -> IMPLEMENT -> TEST -> INTEGRATE -> RUN -> ACCEPT -> REPAIR -> TEST -> ACCEPT -> COMMIT -> PUSH -> REPLAN`

Use `npm run product:cline:audit` as the first full-platform review command, then `npm run product:factory` as the primary local acceptance command.

## Full-platform review
For a product-affecting task, run `npm run product:cline:audit` before changing code. Review the complete surface: architecture, capabilities, engine ownership, APIs, UI/dashboard, persistence, security, Windows/Web/Android runtime, tests, CI workflows, packaging, release scripts, and deployment contracts. The audit writes `.hooshyar/cline-platform-audit.json` and maps every required Qualification Matrix cell to static status. Static review never upgrades a runtime/acceptance/CI cell to PASS.

## Repair behavior
When the factory returns BLOCKED:
- first run `npm run product:factory:handoff`;
- treat the emitted `ASSISTANT_REPAIR_MISSION` as the canonical repair input;
- identify the first failing stage, Matrix cell, environment, workflow, and root cause;
- make the smallest coherent repair;
- never weaken/remove a failing test to obtain green;
- never modify Architecture Freeze V4 to bypass a failure;
- add or update a regression test for the repaired defect;
- rerun `npm run product:cline:audit`;
- rerun focused verification;
- rerun `npm run product:factory`;
- after application acceptance passes, run `npm test -- --runInBand`.

## Product acceptance
A green engine/unit test is not commercial completion. The real Windows journey must pass:
`health -> ready -> session -> tenant -> ingestion -> financial analysis -> dashboard -> restart -> same tenant -> restored dashboard`.

Equivalent customer workflows must be proven for Web and Android before those environments are marked PASS.

## Evidence protocol
Every finding must contain:
- severity
- evidence source
- Manifest layer
- Qualification Matrix cell
- environment
- workflow
- root cause
- required change
- regression verification
- acceptance verification
- release impact

Unknown is not PASS. BLOCKED is not PASS. Passing one environment never proves another environment.

## Git discipline
Before risky changes create a checkpoint/commit when possible. Keep one coherent capability/fix per commit. Do not force-push. Do not push or merge unless the repository policy explicitly permits it.

## Cline boundary
Cline may execute commands, inspect the repository and GitHub evidence available through configured tooling, apply the smallest implementation repair, and run verification. Cline must not invent a new engine, duplicate business semantics, or claim product completion without application and acceptance evidence.
